  rejects a zero-sized bridge buffer at construction [✔]
  rethrows the worker exception to the consumer when the worker dies [✔]
  ends the stream after a clean worker stop [✔]
  cancelAction returns promptly even when the bridge queue is full [✔]
  cancelAction is idempotent and leaves no subscription thread registered [✔]
stream history guard
  returns exact metadata and pages with production cursor semantics [✔]
  returns typed unavailable results for missing and reserved streams [✔]
  returns soft-deleted metadata and blocks undelete until guard completion [✔]
  blocks append until guard completion [✔]
  releases the guard on rollback and lets the blocked append complete [✔]
  blocks link into the guarded stream until guard completion [✔]
  blocks soft delete and logical truncate until guard completion [✔]
  blocks hard delete of the guarded origin until guard completion [✔]
  blocks hard delete of another origin linked into the guarded stream [✔]
  keeps opposing hard deletes and multi-stream appends deadlock-free [✔]
InterpreterHooks
  enrichEvent
    applies enrichEvent to appended events surfaced through readStreamForward [✔]
    applies enrichEvent across appendMultiStream per-stream batches [✔]
  decodeHook
    retains the no-hook batch without evaluating its events [✔]
    applies decodeHook to readAllForward results [✔]
    applies decodeHook to subscription handlers across catch-up and live phases [✔]
  no hooks
    with defaultStoreSettings, a round-trip preserves payload and metadata exactly [✔]
findCausationDescendants
  returns the seed event and every descendant in global-position order [✔]
  on an eventId with no descendants returns a vector of length 1 (the seed only) [✔]
  on a non-existent eventId returns an empty vector [✔]
findCausationAncestors
  walks from a leaf back to the root, leaf first [✔]
findByCorrelation
  returns every event with the given correlation across multiple streams in global-position order [✔]
  on an unknown correlation returns an empty vector [✔]
ConsumerGroupSql
  category consumer-group partitioning (size 4)
    splits a category into 4 pairwise-disjoint member slices [✔]
    union of all member slices equals the unpartitioned category read [✔]
    every stream's events go to exactly one member, in ascending global position [✔]
    member assignment is deterministic across repeated reads [✔]
    size 1 is equivalent to an unpartitioned category read [✔]
  per-member checkpoints
    stores and reads independent checkpoints per member [✔]
    never moves a member checkpoint backward (GREATEST monotonicity) [✔]
    missing member checkpoint reads as Nothing [✔]
    the existing name-keyed checkpoint statements still round-trip (as member 0) [✔]
  $all consumer-group partitioning (size 4)
    splits $all into 4 pairwise-disjoint member slices [✔]
    union of all member slices equals the unpartitioned $all read [✔]
    every stream's events go to exactly one member, in ascending global position [✔]
    size 1 is equivalent to an unpartitioned $all read [✔]
  member_of assignment rule
    returns a member index in [0, size) for every stream [✔]
consumer-group resize
  rejects invalid sizes and member indices at construction [✔]
  refuses a configured size that disagrees with stored topology before creating a member [✔]
  also refuses an ordinary subscription over an existing larger group [✔]
  refuses an underestimated derived topology until resized [✔]
  refuses mixed stored sizes even when its own row agrees [✔]
  serializes concurrent initializers with competing group sizes [✔]
  persists configured topology on initialization, ordinary saves and dead-letter saves [✔]
  delivers every seeded event after equalizing size 2 to size 3 [✔]
  is idempotent when repeated at the same size and retains surviving member identities [✔]
  starts a missing group at zero and removes obsolete members on shrink [✔]
  rolls back the complete resize with the caller transaction [✔]
consumer groups
  delivers a disjoint, complete, per-stream-ordered partition (size-4 category group) [✔]
  size-1 group delivers the same set as a plain subscription [✔]
  $all group partitions the whole store across members [✔]
  resumes member 2 from its own (name, member) checkpoint [✔]
  lifecycle events carry the consumer-group member context (GroupMember 2 4) [✔]
  consumerGroupGuard fails fast when another holder holds the (name, member) lock [✔]
  subscriptionStream forwards the consumer-group field (member 0 of 2 sees its slice) [✔]
consumer groups (effectful)
  routes each member through the effectful API to its own disjoint, complete, per-stream-ordered slice (size-2 category group) [✔]
  preserves State across handler calls within one member (Persistent unlift) [✔]
performance structure
  no-op paths use no pooled connection
    rejects invalid dead-letter page sizes before pool checkout [✔]
    rejects invalid batch and buffer sizes before pool checkout [✔]
    rejects invalid consumer-group values before pool checkout [✔]
    refuses mismatched topology in exactly one initialization checkout with no handler [✔]
    refuses mismatched target in exactly one initialization checkout with no handler [✔]
    keeps ordinary checkpoint saves as one unconditional monotonic upsert [✔]
    rejects an empty appendToStream batch before pool checkout [✔]
    returns an empty appendMultiStream result before pool checkout [✔]
    rejects invalid retention requests before pool checkout [✔]
    keeps every ordinary statement free of retention coordination [✔]
  production query plans
    visible global head lookup uses ux_stream_events_stream_version without Sort [✔]
    dead-letter reads use ix_dead_letters_subscription_position without Sort [✔]
    orphan dead-letter cleanup uses ix_dead_letters_event_id [✔]
    active retention lookup uses ix_history_retention_leases_unreleased_expiry [✔]
    installs no retention trigger for INSERT or UPDATE [✔]
  dead-letter production query plans
